  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape is currently dominated by the countdown to the September 15, 2026, Senate vote on the CLARITY Act, a structural watershed for U.S. regulatory oversight. While legislative certainty is poised to unlock advanced native Bitcoin programmability and non-custodial cross-chain liquidity, the institutional ETF sector has entered a pronounced 'Fatigue' phase. New data indicates the first calendar year of net outflows for Bitcoin ETFs in H1 2026 and the first major corporate treasury sales, signaling a transition from pure accumulation to a utility-driven market. This environment is accelerating the development of Bitcoin-native execution layers that directly challenge the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) for dApp dominance.",
